<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="F_AttenuatorOK" Id="{860b1a67-b309-4c7c-986b-4453f9f031c8}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
Indicates if the attenuator can be considered safe for a device,
given its status word.

In local mode, the atteunator ignores PMPS requests, following a local
setpoint. In this mode, a device cannot trust that the attenuator will not
increase transmission beyond its own setpoint. Therefore any
indication of a changing transmission should cause a fault.

In PMPS mode, if a device has submitted a preemptive request and received
acknowledgement, then the transmission setpoint will be governed at least
by that device's setpoint. Therefore, the attenuator may be moving without
generating a fault.

The status-word bit map is not written out here: the bit positions are the
named constants PMPS_GVL.ATT_STATUS_AT_TARGET, ATT_STATUS_MOVING,
ATT_STATUS_LOCAL_MODE, ATT_STATUS_PMPS_MODE and ATT_STATUS_OK, whose layout
matches the BIT members of ST_AttenuatorStatus. Change the bit map there, in
one place, and this function follows.

HISTORY
    2020-11-05 / Alex Wallace
        Function created with the transmission (BP) compare change; status
        bits were selected with numeric literals.
    2026-11-27 / Scirix Agent
        Replaced the numeric status-bit selectors with the named status-bit
        constants declared in PMPS_GVL. Logic and result are unchanged (audit
        finding #269, convention conv_a8288970c008).
*)
FUNCTION F_AttenuatorOK : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    xStatus : WORD; // Attenuator status word, bit map PMPS_GVL.ATT_STATUS_* (layout of ST_AttenuatorStatus)
END_VAR
VAR
    xAtTarget  : BOOL; // Status bit 0: attenuator has reached its requested transmission
    xMoving    : BOOL; // Status bit 1: attenuator is moving to a new transmission
    xLocalMode : BOOL; // Status bit 2: local mode, PMPS requests ignored
    xPMPSMode  : BOOL; // Status bit 3: PMPS mode, setpoints taken only from PMPS
    xOK        : BOOL; // Status bit 4: no attenuator error, status is stable
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[// Decode the status word through the named bit map in PMPS_GVL so the
// decision logic below reads by name rather than by bit position.
xAtTarget  := (xStatus AND PMPS_GVL.ATT_STATUS_AT_TARGET) <> 0;
xMoving    := (xStatus AND PMPS_GVL.ATT_STATUS_MOVING) <> 0;
xLocalMode := (xStatus AND PMPS_GVL.ATT_STATUS_LOCAL_MODE) <> 0;
xPMPSMode  := (xStatus AND PMPS_GVL.ATT_STATUS_PMPS_MODE) <> 0;
xOK        := (xStatus AND PMPS_GVL.ATT_STATUS_OK) <> 0;

IF xLocalMode THEN // Local mode
    F_AttenuatorOK := xAtTarget AND NOT xMoving;
ELSIF xPMPSMode AND NOT xLocalMode THEN // PMPS mode
    F_AttenuatorOK := TRUE;
END_IF

F_AttenuatorOK := xOK AND F_AttenuatorOK;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>